node_modules/
dist/
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/binaries/

# `src-tauri/gen/android/` is generated by `tauri android init` and then
# committed, against the usual advice, because we edit parts of it: the
# manifest, `MainActivity.kt`, the Gradle config. A generated file you edit is
# source.
#
# Which parts those are is not decided here. `tauri android init` writes its
# own `.gitignore` files into that folder, and they already separate what it
# regenerates every build — the `generated/` Kotlin, the built `.so`, the
# `tauri.*` files — from what is left for us. Repeating any of it here would
# be a second opinion that goes stale the next time Tauri changes its mind.
#
# Only this is ours to say, because a signing key is not Tauri's problem:
src-tauri/gen/android/**/*.jks
src-tauri/gen/android/**/*.keystore
